

(assert (equalp (loop for spec in '("~(~A~)"  "~:(~A~)" "~@(~A~)" "~:@(~A~)") 
                       collect (format nil "~@?" spec "hello cruel world!"))
                '("hello cruel world!"
                  "Hello Cruel World!"
                  "Hello cruel world!"
                  "HELLO CRUEL WORLD!")))

is not fullfilled in bocl.
It should.

== RESOLVED (v1.5.8) ==
The FORMAT ~(...~) case-conversion directive was unimplemented (the ~( and ~)
directives were silently ignored, so no case folding happened) and ~@? was broken
(it always popped an args-LIST, giving a type error / NIL).  Fixed in printer.c
(bocl_format_run):
- New ~(...~) handler (CLHS 22.3.8.2): runs the inner control into a string buffer
  (consuming args in place), then folds it — ~( downcase, ~:( capitalize each word,
  ~@( capitalize the first word (rest lower), ~:@( upcase — and emits it; new
  fmt_find_close_paren finds the matching ~) honouring nesting; ~) ends the block.
- ~@? now checks the @ modifier: ~? pops a control string + a LIST of args (as
  before); ~@? pops the control string and consumes the REMAINING args in place.
The issue's assertion now holds; new test_format "format ~(...~)/~@?".  Full unit
suite (42) green.
